; The Yandex Music addon's settings, as the addon writes them on the card:
;
;     <card>/Addons/yandex/settings.ini
;
; One "key = value" per line; comments and blank lines are ignored. The addon
; reads the file at start and on "read again from the card" in its screen, so a
; hand edit is enough -- nothing needs rebuilding.
;
; The four keys are the official Yandex Music client's and are nobody else's to
; publish: the Music API has no developer program, and nothing is compiled into
; the player. A file that does not carry all four is "no keys" on the addon's
; screen and the service stays off (yandexconf.h, yandex_configured()).
;
; Where the four values come from, and how they are checked, is in
; docs/ADDONS.md, "yandex". Two rules matter:
;
;   - sign_key and client_header are a pair from the same client. The signature
;     of get-file-info is checked together with that header, so a key from the
;     Android app next to a desktop header is refused;
;   - client_header carries the client's version and it ages: when playback
;     starts being refused, bump the version before suspecting the key.
;
; This file is an example and is not packed: `make addons-pack` copies an
; addon's *.ini files to the card, so a real settings.ini must never sit in this
; directory -- it would ship the keys with the build and overwrite the card's.

client_id =
client_secret =
sign_key =
client_header =

; lossless (the default), high or normal -- a ceiling, not a promise: what the
; account may have decides the rest (yandex.c, QUALITIES).
quality = lossless

; Where the API and the OAuth endpoint are, when they are not the real ones
; (a mock, or a mirror). Left out, the defaults stand.
; base_url = https://api.music.yandex.net
; auth_url = https://oauth.yandex.ru
